  "notes": "Drawn from N795CK (777F, 2025, left side) and checked against N778CK (777-300ERSF) and N708CK (747-400F) from the right. The 747-400Fs and 767s wear the same scheme. Several Kalitta 777Fs fly in full DHL paint (tagged in airframes/CKS.json as BCS/standard); N772CK has been seen with Kalitta titles forward and a DHL-yellow aft fuselage and tail (a hybrid, not drawn). Re-checked 2026-11-15 against N795CK (777F, 2025-08-09) and N778CK (2025-10-24): the title's place, cap height and length (0.25) agree with both; the fuselage and fin bands are straight-edged (corners only), so nothing moved.",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximate standard (a few colors from memory). The red and gold tail and 'KALITTA AIR' titles date from the airline's 2000 re-formation (from American International Airways)."
